# Review after code changes

After implementing or fixing code, review the diff before handing it back.

- Important issues change the agreed approach, acceptance, data, or permission boundary. Stop and let the user decide. Do not implement that change while waiting.
- Fix every other confirmed defect directly. Add a regression test, run the relevant checks, and review the final diff. Report remaining limitations and blockers candidly.
- Ask only when necessary information or a product decision is missing and cannot be resolved from the specification or existing authorization; continue independent work while waiting.
- Record causes, fixes, and verification in the corresponding Jira issue when requested. If the connector fails, report the failure instead of claiming synchronization.
- Do not edit plan files unless the user explicitly authorizes plan changes.
- Do not commit or push a review-driven fix unless the user already asked to commit.
